    "explanation": "Both accounts agree on the shape of this dispute, and the record resolves it. The deviation is measured under POL-RD-22 on the platform's recorded distances, not on the sparse trace: the trip record shows 18.3 km actually driven against 15.7 km on the recommended route, a deviation of 2.60 km (16.6%), which is over the 1.0 km tolerance. The GPS trace is not used to re-measure distance, but it confirms which route was taken — the vehicle left the recommended Pan-Island Expressway routing at the Pasir Ris Drive 3 / TPE slip road at 14:18:56, ran the TPE and then Braddell Road, and rejoined at Toa Payoh Lorong 6 at 14:40:41.\n\nOn traffic justification (POL-RD-23), the driver's explanation does not hold. The only advisory in the record is a ROADWORK on the PIE (towards Tuas) after Tampines Avenue 10 exit, and its validity window is 2026-09-05 23:00 to 2026-09-06 05:00 — the trip ran 14:16–14:42, so the advisory does not overlap the trip window and does not justify the reroute. POL-RD-23 is explicit that a driver's bare assertion of traffic, with no overlapping traffic data, does not justify a reroute. The driver's statement of roadworks is therefore noted but not accepted as a justification.\n\nOn notice (POL-RD-21), the chat log is contiguous with 0 messages, the trip record's in-app calls and messages_during_trip are empty, and there is no call recording in the record. A verbal notice with no recording cannot be established. The driver did not give recorded notice of the deviation.\n\nApplying the POL-RD-24 matrix: the deviation is over tolerance, so rows (c) and (e) are closed; row (a) requires the rider to have been informed and to have agreed, which the empty chat log forecloses; and the reroute is not traffic-justified, so the case falls in row (d) — not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km — which refunds the excess distance fare in full. That fare is the deviation distance times the per-km rate, without surge: 2.60 km × 0.72 SGD = 1.87 SGD, rounded to the cent. This is the whole monetary remedy the matrix provides; it is not the 6.00 SGD claimed, because POL-RD-24 returns the excess distance fare and not the trip fare, and it is not a NO_ACTION, because the deviation exceeded tolerance with no traffic justification. The rider is carrying the charge (total_charged 21.56 SGD, refund_issued_sgd 0.0), so a PARTIAL_REFUND of 1.87 SGD returns that part of the trip's charge.\n\nOn who decides: the contested amount is 6.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries a fraud flag and no safety flag is set, so the AI ruling is final on that clause; POL-RD-25's own 0.80 confidence requirement is met, and its extra 2 km limb is switched off because route_deviation.thresholds.ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false. Every artifact this ruling rests on — the trip record, the GPS trace, the fare breakdown and the traffic advisory — is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no fact is left unestablished and POL-GEN-26 does not require escalation.",
